The Parent section provides the foundational context and introduces key concepts such as the pass-efficient model, sparse-unordered representation of data, and the Select algorithm. It also mentions a proof for Lemma 1 which is crucial to understanding how the Select Algorithm works in one pass over the data stream. This part sets up the theoretical framework that will be further expanded upon by Child 2 and Child 3.

Child 2: 40%
This section delves deeper into the specifics of the Select algorithm, providing a detailed explanation of its operation and proof for Lemma 1. It also introduces an extension to this lemma in the form of Lemma 2 which deals with selecting row labels from matrices presented in sparse-unordered representation. This part is essential as it provides practical applications and extensions of the concepts introduced by the parent section, hence a higher percentage.

Child 3: 40%
This child discusses sampling lemmas that are crucial for understanding how to sample elements according to certain probability distributions using the Select algorithm in one pass over the data stream. It also introduces Lemma 2 which is an extension of Lemma 1, allowing selection from a sparse-unordered representation of matrices. This section provides important details on implementing these algorithms and their applications, hence it's given equal importance as Child 2.
